#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:1
msgid "Spawn URDF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:3
msgid ""
"This tutorial will cover how to spawn a URDF model in Gazebo Sim. URDF files "
"are often used in ROS to represent robot models. While SDF can describe a "
"world with multiple robot models, URDF can only describe one robot model. "
"More information about URDF can be found at [https://wiki.ros.org/urdf]"
"(https://wiki.ros.org/urdf)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:8
msgid "Obtaining a URDF file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:10
msgid ""
"This tutorial assumes that the reader already has a URDF file that they'd "
"like to load into Gazebo Sim. If you are looking for a URDF file to use, you "
"can use the [`rrbot.urdf`](https://github.com/gazebosim/docs/blob/master/"
"fortress/tutorials/spawn_urdf/rrbot.urdf) that was preprocessed for you. The "
"`rrbot` robot model is from the [`gazebo_ros_demos`](https://github.com/ros-"
"simulation/gazebo_ros_demos) package. You could also use one of the examples "
"listed at [https://wiki.ros.org/urdf/Examples](https://wiki.ros.org/urdf/"
"Examples)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:13
msgid ""
"If you have a `xacro` representation of a robot model, you can turn the "
"`xacro` file into a `URDF` file using the [`xacro`](https://index.ros.org/p/"
"xacro/) package: see [this tutorial](https://docs.ros.org/en/foxy/Tutorials/"
"URDF/Using-Xacro-to-Clean-Up-a-URDF-File.html) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:15
msgid "Spawning the URDF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:17
msgid ""
"To spawn a URDF model in Gazebo Sim, we will start a world and make use of "
"the world's `create` service, which uses the [EntityFactory](https://"
"gazebosim.org/api/msgs/8/classignition_1_1msgs_1_1EntityFactory.html) "
"message type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:19
msgid "Start by launching an empty world in Gazebo Sim:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:20
msgid "ign gazebo empty.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:24
msgid "You should see a window that looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:26
msgid "![empty_world](tutorials/spawn_urdf/empty_world.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:26
msgid "empty_world"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:28
msgid ""
"In another terminal, get the list of available services by running `ign "
"service -l`. Look for a `create` service. You should see this service in the "
"list:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:31
msgid "/world/empty/create\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:35
msgid ""
"We can double-check that this is the service we want to use by running `ign "
"service -is /world/empty/create`. This will show us the service's request "
"and response message types:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:37
msgid "ignition.msgs.EntityFactory, ignition.msgs.Boolean\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:41
msgid ""
"Now that we have found the service that has an `EntityFactory` request type, "
"we can call this service and pass the URDF file to the service's request so "
"that the robot represented by this URDF file is spawned in the Gazebo Sim "
"world. We do this by setting the desired URDF file to the `sdf_file_name` "
"field of the `EntityFactory` request message. The [libsdformat](https://"
"gazebosim.org/libs/sdformat) library will then internally convert the URDF "
"file to an SDF representation, and load this into the running world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:45
msgid ""
"The following command spawns the URDF file `model.urdf` into the Gazebo Sim "
"world as a model named `urdf_model`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:46
msgid ""
"ign service -s /world/empty/create --reqtype ignition.msgs.EntityFactory --"
"reptype ignition.msgs.Boolean --timeout 1000 --req 'sdf_filename: \"/path/to/"
"model.urdf\", name: \"urdf_model\"'\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:50
msgid ""
"If `model.urdf` is the URDF representation of [rrbot.xacro](https://github."
"com/ros-simulation/gazebo_ros_demos/blob/kinetic-devel/rrbot_description/"
"urdf/rrbot.xacro) in the `gazebo_ros_demos` package, executing the service "
"call above should result in a simulation that now looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:52
msgid "![urdf_spawned](tutorials/spawn_urdf/urdf_spawned.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:52
msgid "urdf_spawned"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../spawn_urdf.md:54
msgid ""
"We can now play the simulation to make sure that the loaded URDF model "
"behaves as expected:"
msgstr ""

